WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.954 --> 00:00:08.892
♪ ♪

00:00:07.223 --> 00:00:10.260
&gt;&gt; Juan: A NEW JERSEY

00:00:09.025 --> 00:00:10.860
HIGH SCHOOL UPSETTING STUDENTS

00:00:10.393 --> 00:00:12.295
AND SOME PARENTS AFTER

00:00:10.994 --> 00:00:14.497
IMPLEMENTING A NEW POLICY TO

00:00:12.429 --> 00:00:15.098
MAKE THE CHEERLEADING TEAM MORE

00:00:14.631 --> 00:00:17.300
INCLUSIVE.

00:00:15.231 --> 00:00:18.968
THE SCHOOL SAYING THE SQUAD MUST

00:00:17.434 --> 00:00:19.335
NOW ACCEPT EVERYONE OR BE

00:00:19.102 --> 00:00:21.204
DISBANDED.

00:00:19.469 --> 00:00:22.906
THIS DECISION COMING UP TO ONE

00:00:21.337 --> 00:00:25.508
PARENT COMPLAINED WHEN HER CHILD

00:00:23.039 --> 00:00:26.309
DIDN'T MAKE THE CUT FOLLOWING

00:00:25.642 --> 00:00:29.612
TRYOUTS LAST MONTH.

00:00:26.443 --> 00:00:31.481
GREG, IS THIS A CASE OF, YOU

00:00:29.746 --> 00:00:33.283
KNOW, --

00:00:31.614 --> 00:00:33.683
&gt;&gt; Kimberly: HE WAS A

00:00:33.416 --> 00:00:35.285
CHEERLEADER.

00:00:33.817 --> 00:00:36.319
&gt;&gt; Greg: I WAS.

00:00:35.418 --> 00:00:37.720
&gt;&gt; Juan: IS THAT RIGHT?

00:00:36.453 --> 00:00:43.093
I DIDN'T KNOW IF YOU ARE HAVING

00:00:37.854 --> 00:00:45.095
FUN AT HIS EXPENSE.

00:00:43.226 --> 00:00:46.029
&gt;&gt; Greg: A SECRET I WAS TRYING

00:00:45.228 --> 00:00:47.730
TO KEEP FROM AMERICA.

00:00:46.162 --> 00:00:50.133
&gt;&gt; Juan: DO YOU THINK IT'S

00:00:47.864 --> 00:00:51.901
WEAKENING OUR CHILDREN?

00:00:50.266 --> 00:00:52.702
&gt;&gt; Greg: I DON'T KNOW.

00:00:52.035 --> 00:00:55.038
HERE IS MY FEELING.

00:00:52.836 --> 00:00:57.407
IT'S A SMALL LOCAL STORY OVER A

00:00:55.171 --> 00:01:00.310
BEEF OVER A CHEERLEADING CHOICE.

00:00:57.540 --> 00:01:02.312
SOME PARENTS CUT TICKED OFF.

00:01:00.443 --> 00:01:03.513
NOW IT'S A NATIONAL STORY.

00:01:02.445 --> 00:01:04.814
I'M A LITTLE SCARED.

00:01:03.646 --> 00:01:05.849
NONE OF THE TEACHERS OR COACHES

00:01:04.948 --> 00:01:09.085
MAKE ENOUGH MONEY TO BE FORCED

00:01:05.982 --> 00:01:11.121
TO DEAL WITH THE TRANSIENT

00:01:09.219 --> 00:01:11.788
SPOTLIGHT SEEKING THE LATEST RAW

00:01:11.621 --> 00:01:12.489
MEAT.

00:01:11.921 --> 00:01:14.524
I FEEL AMBIVALENT.

00:01:12.622 --> 00:01:16.459
I KNOW I AM NOT SUPPOSED TO.

00:01:14.657 --> 00:01:19.696
THIS IS A TERRIBLE STORY!

00:01:16.593 --> 00:01:21.397
I AM OUTRAGED!

00:01:19.829 --> 00:01:21.698
POLITICAL CORRECTNESS RUN A

00:01:21.531 --> 00:01:23.733
MOCK.

00:01:21.831 --> 00:01:25.602
&gt;&gt; Jesse: THAT'S WHAT YOU

00:01:23.867 --> 00:01:28.204
WANTED.

00:01:25.735 --> 00:01:31.307
&gt;&gt; Kimberly: SOMETIMES...

00:01:28.338 --> 00:01:32.575
PERCOLATING BELOW THE SURFACE.

00:01:31.441 --> 00:01:34.210
&gt;&gt; Juan: FIVE HOPEFULS WHO

00:01:32.709 --> 00:01:36.880
DIDN'T MAKE IT BECAUSE THEY

00:01:34.344 --> 00:01:39.916
DIDN'T SCORE 87 OR HIGHER, BUT

00:01:37.013 --> 00:01:41.851
THEY DID SCORE 78 TO 86.

00:01:40.049 --> 00:01:42.218
THE SCHOOL SAID YOU CAN FOR

00:01:41.985 --> 00:01:44.521
DISSIPATE.

00:01:42.352 --> 00:01:46.322
&gt;&gt; Dana: OKAY.

00:01:44.654 --> 00:01:47.357
I AM NOT OUTRAGED.

00:01:46.456 --> 00:01:47.757
IT TAKES A LOT TO GET ME

00:01:47.490 --> 00:01:49.559
OUTRAGED.

00:01:47.891 --> 00:01:50.693
BUT I WILL SAY THEY'RE NOT DOING

00:01:49.692 --> 00:01:52.962
THEM ANY FAVORS FOR WHEN THEY

00:01:50.827 --> 00:01:53.329
ARE GOING TO ENTER THE JOB

00:01:53.096 --> 00:01:54.397
MARKETS.

00:01:53.463 --> 00:01:56.299
IT'S A SUPER COMPETITIVE WORLD

00:01:54.531 --> 00:01:57.133
RIGHT NOW TO GET A JOB.

00:01:56.432 --> 00:01:58.735
GUESS WHAT.

00:01:57.267 --> 00:02:02.505
20 PEOPLE DON'T GET THE JOB.

00:01:58.868 --> 00:02:04.107
ONE PERSON WILL GET THE JOB.

00:02:02.639 --> 00:02:06.709
&gt;&gt; Greg: GOOD POINT.

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:07.443
AS A FORMER CHEERLEADER, YES.

00:02:06.843 --> 00:02:09.112
I AGREE.

00:02:07.577 --> 00:02:10.713
&gt;&gt; Juan: JESSE, WHAT ABOUT

00:02:09.245 --> 00:02:12.415
POSITIVE REINFORCEMENT, LIKE

00:02:10.847 --> 00:02:14.317
SAYING TO YOUNG PEOPLE, YEAH, WE

00:02:12.549 --> 00:02:14.651
ARE GOING TO REWARD YOU FOR YOUR

00:02:14.450 --> 00:02:15.818
EFFORT.

00:02:14.784 --> 00:02:17.120
&gt;&gt; Jesse: IF EVERYBODY MAKES

00:02:15.952 --> 00:02:19.322
THE TEAM, THEN YOU DON'T TRY

00:02:17.253 --> 00:02:20.423
HARD TO MAKE THE TEAM.

00:02:19.455 --> 00:02:22.325
&gt;&gt; Juan: NO, I WAS SAYING EVEN

00:02:20.557 --> 00:02:24.561
PEOPLE WHO ARE TRYING BUT DON'T

00:02:22.458 --> 00:02:26.162
MAKE THE CUT ARE BEING

00:02:24.694 --> 00:02:26.596
ENCOURAGED TO CONTINUE

00:02:26.296 --> 00:02:27.730
PARTICIPATING.

00:02:26.729 --> 00:02:29.332
&gt;&gt; Jesse: TOO BAD.

00:02:27.864 --> 00:02:32.335
THAT'S WHY THEY HAVE THE TEAM.

00:02:29.465 --> 00:02:32.602
YOU MAKE IT OR YOU DON'T MAKE

00:02:32.468 --> 00:02:33.736
IT.

00:02:32.735 --> 00:02:35.505
I HATE THIS STORY.

00:02:33.870 --> 00:02:36.706
I THINK IT'S TOTALLY LAME.

00:02:35.638 --> 00:02:37.307
WHEN WE WERE GROWING UP, THERE

00:02:36.839 --> 00:02:38.007
WERE CUTS.

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:41.110
YOU FOUND OUT.

00:02:38.141 --> 00:02:41.578
YOU WOULD LOOK ON THE SHEET.

00:02:41.244 --> 00:02:47.116
YOU DIDN'T PLAY.

00:02:41.711 --> 00:02:48.518
SORRY, MAYBE NEXT YEAR.

00:02:47.250 --> 00:02:49.252
&gt;&gt; Dana: THAT ARE DETECTED.

00:02:48.651 --> 00:02:51.254
THEN YOU DON'T HAVE TO WALK UP

00:02:49.385 --> 00:02:52.922
AND LOOK.

00:02:51.387 --> 00:02:53.323
&gt;&gt; Jesse: PEOPLE LOOK AND THEN

00:02:53.056 --> 00:02:55.959
SCURRY AWAY.

00:02:53.456 --> 00:02:56.526
&gt;&gt; Kimberly: DID YOU EVER NOT

00:02:56.092 --> 00:02:58.161
MAKE SOMETHING?

00:02:56.659 --> 00:02:59.095
&gt;&gt; Jesse: I GOT CUT IN

00:02:58.294 --> 00:03:02.198
EIGHTH GRADE BASKETBALL.

00:02:59.229 --> 00:03:03.199
BUT I WEASELED MY WAY ONTO THE

00:03:02.332 --> 00:03:05.268
TEAM.

00:03:03.333 --> 00:03:07.937
&gt;&gt; Juan: MICHAEL JORDAN GOT

00:03:05.401 --> 00:03:09.105
CUT.

00:03:08.071 --> 00:03:11.274
MICHAEL JORDAN DIDN'T QUIT.

00:03:09.239 --> 00:03:12.709
THIS IS REALLY INTERESTING,

00:03:11.407 --> 00:03:13.910
KIMBERLY.

00:03:12.842 --> 00:03:14.777
&gt;&gt; Kimberly: THAT GREG IS A

00:03:14.043 --> 00:03:16.346
CHEERLEADER AND NOT ME.

00:03:14.911 --> 00:03:17.614
&gt;&gt; Juan: I THINK YOU COULD

00:03:16.479 --> 00:03:21.918
HAVE BEEN IF YOU WANTED TO.

00:03:17.747 --> 00:03:22.752
THERE'S A DIFFERENCE BETWEEN

00:03:22.051 --> 00:03:25.355
DANCE AND ART FOR CHEERLEADING

00:03:22.885 --> 00:03:26.723
AND ACROBATIC CHEERLEADERS.

00:03:25.488 --> 00:03:27.023
&gt;&gt; Jesse: JUAN IS IN THE

00:03:26.856 --> 00:03:28.091
WEEDS.

00:03:27.156 --> 00:03:28.524
&gt;&gt; Juan: WHO GETS POINTS AND

00:03:28.224 --> 00:03:31.294
WHO DOESN'T.

00:03:28.658 --> 00:03:32.929
DOESN'T MAKE A BIG DIFFERENCE.

00:03:31.427 --> 00:03:34.297
&gt;&gt; Kimberly: WHAT HAPPENS IS,

00:03:33.062 --> 00:03:35.531
SOMETIMES YOU CAN HAVE, WE USED

00:03:34.430 --> 00:03:37.734
TO HAVE AT MY SCHOOL.

00:03:35.665 --> 00:03:38.301
WE HAD SONG GIRLS AND WE HAD

00:03:37.867 --> 00:03:40.903
CHEERLEADERS.

00:03:38.434 --> 00:03:43.072
THE CHEERLEADERS WOULD DO MORE

00:03:41.037 --> 00:03:44.907
ACROBATICS, TUMBLING.

00:03:43.206 --> 00:03:45.308
SONG GIRLS DID THE DANCE

00:03:45.041 --> 00:03:46.476
ROUTINE.

00:03:45.441 --> 00:03:48.811
IT WAS KIND OF SEPARATE.

00:03:46.609 --> 00:03:50.146
YOU ALSO HAVE TO BE IN VERY GOOD

00:03:48.945 --> 00:03:50.446
PHYSICAL SHAPE TO BE ABLE TO DO

00:03:50.280 --> 00:03:52.715
THIS.

00:03:50.580 --> 00:03:53.116
PYRAMIDS AND STUFF AND YOU CAN

00:03:52.849 --> 00:03:53.816
FALL.

00:03:53.249 --> 00:03:56.219
THEY DO FLIPS.

00:03:53.950 --> 00:03:58.354
IT'S NOT THE EASIEST THING.

00:03:56.352 --> 00:04:00.323
YOU'VE GOT TO BE IN SHAPE TO BE

00:03:58.488 --> 00:04:01.557
ABLE TO DO IT.

00:04:00.456 --> 00:04:01.891
&gt;&gt; Jesse: ISN'T CHEERLEADING

00:04:01.691 --> 00:04:03.960
SEXIST?

00:04:02.025 --> 00:04:05.528
THIS IS THE WHOLE THING.

00:04:04.093 --> 00:04:06.629
WHAT ARE LIBERALS DOING?

00:04:05.662 --> 00:04:08.131
COERCING YOUNG GIRLS.

00:04:06.763 --> 00:04:09.265
&gt;&gt; Juan: HOW DO YOU KNOW THE

00:04:08.264 --> 00:04:11.200
PRINCIPLE IS A LIBERAL?

00:04:09.399 --> 00:04:12.535
&gt;&gt; Jesse: OH, COME ON.

00:04:11.334 --> 00:04:14.237
&gt;&gt; Kimberly: I DON'T KNOW

00:04:12.669 --> 00:04:16.739
WHERE HE WENT WITH THIS.

00:04:14.370 --> 00:04:18.374
WHEN I WAS IN SECOND GRADE,

00:04:16.873 --> 00:04:19.509
THERE WAS NO GIRLS TEAM FOR

00:04:18.508 --> 00:04:20.376
SOCCER.

00:04:19.642 --> 00:04:21.911
MY MOM CONVINCED THE COACH TO

00:04:20.510 --> 00:04:23.446
GIVE ME A TRYOUT AND SAID IF SHE

00:04:22.045 --> 00:04:25.214
IS GOOD ENOUGH AND SHE IS AS

00:04:23.579 --> 00:04:26.749
GOOD AS ANY OF THE GUYS PLAYING,

00:04:25.348 --> 00:04:28.484
THEN PUT HER ON THE TEAM.

00:04:26.883 --> 00:04:30.520
IF SHE'S NOT, CUT HER.

00:04:28.618 --> 00:04:31.721
I MADE THE TEAM.

00:04:30.653 --> 00:04:33.790
I LIKED IT.

00:04:31.854 --> 00:04:35.558
IT TAUGHT ME TO RELINE HER SOFT,

00:04:33.923 --> 00:04:37.193
PRACTICE, WORK HARD AND DO IT.

00:04:35.692 --> 00:04:37.727
EVENTUALLY THEY HAD A GIRLS

00:04:37.327 --> 00:04:39.128
TEAM.

00:04:37.860 --> 00:04:41.564
&gt;&gt; Greg: DO YOU REMEMBER ON

00:04:39.262 --> 00:04:43.733
THE BRADY BUNCH WHEN PETER BRADY

00:04:41.698 --> 00:04:44.901
BECAME A SUNFLOWER, GIRL SCOUTS.

00:04:43.866 --> 00:04:45.902
THEN MARCIA BRADY JOINED THE

00:04:45.635 --> 00:04:49.238
GIRL SCOUTS.

00:04:46.035 --> 00:04:52.375
THAT WAS IN THE EARLY '70s.

00:04:49.372 --> 00:04:53.710
&gt;&gt; Jesse: HOW OLD ARE YOU?

